--TEST--
The value a child throws reaches the caller as its own class carrying its own data, from `Core\Task::all` and from `Core\Task::map` alike, and a `catch` for a class it is not does not take it — `rule:concurrency/nothing-is-still-running-when-a-call-returns` and `rule:errors/throwable-hierarchy`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:concurrency/a-child-s-throw
// The agreement shape: one question asked of both group calls, asserting that
// they answer the same way rather than what each answered on its own. A group
// call that wrapped the child's throw would miss the `ImportFailed` arm in
// both, and one that rebuilt it as its supertype would lose `$row`.
class ImportFailed extends RuntimeError {
    public int $row;

    public function constructor(string $message, int $row) {
        parent::constructor($message);
        $this->row = $row;
    }
}

class Runner {
    public static function fromAll(): string {
        try {
            Core\Task::all({
                // Returns at once, so the group has a survivor to cancel and
                // the case is not one child on its own.
                good: fn(): int => {
                    Core\Time::sleep(2s);
                    return 1;
                },
                bad: fn(): int => {
                    throw new ImportFailed("no price", 31);
                },
            });
        } catch (ImportFailed $e) {
            return "all: " . $e->message . " at row " . ($e->row as string);
        }
        return "all: nothing propagated";
    }

    public static function fromMap(): string {
        try {
            Core\Task::map([31, 32], fn(int $n): int => {
                throw new ImportFailed("no price", $n);
            });
        } catch (ImportFailed $e) {
            return "map: " . $e->message;
        }
        return "map: nothing propagated";
    }
}

echo Runner::fromAll(), "\n";
echo Runner::fromMap(), "\n";

// The other side of the bound. A `catch` for a class the throw is not may not
// take it, so "its own class" is asserted from both directions rather than
// read off one arm that happened to match.
try {
    try {
        Core\Task::all({
            bad: fn(): int => {
                throw new ImportFailed("no price", 31);
            },
        });
    } catch (LogicError $wrong) {
        echo "a LogicError catch took it", "\n";
    }
} catch (ImportFailed $right) {
    echo "the LogicError arm let it through", "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
all: no price at row 31
map: no price
the LogicError arm let it through
